# Keep the Semgrep SAST scan on first-party application source. The CI job
# already scopes the scan by passing `apps packages` as explicit targets; this
# file is the belt-and-suspenders equivalent for an ad-hoc `semgrep scan` /
# `semgrep ci` run at the repo root, so those don't drown in the same noise.
#
# Everything below is either vendored (`.claude/skills/*` — third-party skill
# scripts), local tooling (`scripts/`, `tools/`), CI config (`.github/`), or
# root manifests. Scanning them only ever produced false positives and
# opinionated supply-chain/CI policy suggestions — never a real application
# vulnerability (see the 2026-07-29 triage in docs/SECURITY.md).
.claude/
scripts/
tools/
.github/
package.json
pnpm-workspace.yaml
pnpm-lock.yaml
turbo.json
